{"audio":"voiceover.mp3","hash":"22478f9ed1f31602","durationSec":345.365,"text":"ew. Hi guys, welcome to the channel. Today is the big one, what to do with your first ten thousand pounds, or dollars, and how to actually start investing. If you have managed to save ten thousand, first of all, congratulations. That is a massive step. It took me quite some time, mostly because I made a few mistakes on the way. Most finance channels give you the same value, so you know it. If you have managed to save ten thousand, first of all, congratulations. That is a massive step. It took me quite some time, mostly because I made a few mistakes on the way. The same saving, investing, E T F content. You will get that here too. But you will also watch my journey, from the ground up, so you know it is actually possible. My name is Jeffrey. I am an AI consultant at a legal advisory. Before that I worked in private banking for about 2 and a half years. And before that, funnily enough, I dropped out of university, and didn't have any money. a coding bootcamp. That bootcamp landed during a crypto run. I was working at a covid test site at a time on minimum wage and putting about half of what I earned into crypto. And it worked. For a while. I got to about 10, 11, maybe 12 ,000 pounds. Then 2022 happened. I cashed out around four or 5 ,000. Technically a profit. But I had lost most of what I had made. And I lost it because I did not follow the simple rules. I was investing money I could not afford to lose. I had no emergency fund. I had car payments and nothing else to my name. I was young. I was greedy. And I wanted to get rich fast. And if you can get rich fast, you can lose it just as fast. I am not a financial advisor. I am someone who made the mistakes young enough to learn from them without them wrecking my future. So this is the plan I wish someone had handed me. Over the next few weeks this becomes a series. My road to 100 ,000 invested. And after that a million or just work optional. That is the real goal for most of us. Not having to swap your labor for survival. And I am not hiding the numbers. I am on about 55 ,000 base. And somewhere around 63 all in wind bonus. I have also been on 25, 30 and 40. So wherever you are, I have been there. And I can show you what I did at each step. If you want to watch someone do this from the round up, subscribe. And comment what is your number and what are you stuck on. I want this to be a conversation, not a lecture. Right. Here is what to do with the 10 ,000. The plan is not complicated. It is an order. Step one, a starter emergency fund. Step two, kill any vet above roughly 8%. Step three, grab a full employer match. Step four, invest the rest in broad index funds. Step one, not six months of expenses yet. Just one month of their own costs. Part in an easy access savings account you can reach in a pay. This is the thing I did not have, and it is what stops a flat tire becoming credit card bet. Step two is bet. If you are carrying a credit card at 24%, paying it off is a guaranteed 24 % return. No investment gives you that with certainty. So anything above roughly 8 % gets cleared before you invest a pound. Step three, if your job offers a pension match, take all of it. A 50 % match on 6 % of your salary is an instant 50 % return on that money. Nothing else in finance pays that on day one. Step four is where the boring part becomes the exciting part. Left alone in a broad index fund at a 7 % average return. 10 ,000 becomes about 76 ,000 in 30 years. You did not add a single extra pound. Time did the work. 76 ,000 from one decision you made once and then left alone. That is the whole difference between what I did at 22 and what I am doing now. So here is your homework this week. Open an easy access savings account. List every bet you have with its interest rate. Check what your employer match actually is. And open an investment account, even with nothing in it yet. That is the whole order. Emergency fund, expensive bet, earn match, and index funds. This is education, not advice. And it is my own experience. So check your own numbers. If this helped, subscribe. And next week I show you exactly which index funds I picked and why.","words":[{"w":"ew.","s":0.0,"e":0.26},{"w":"Hi","s":0.26,"e":0.26},{"w":"guys,","s":0.26,"e":0.7},{"w":"welcome","s":0.94,"e":1.34},{"w":"to","s":1.34,"e":1.7},{"w":"the","s":1.7,"e":1.94},{"w":"channel.","s":1.94,"e":2.3},{"w":"Today","s":2.8,"e":3.16},{"w":"is","s":3.16,"e":3.46},{"w":"the","s":3.46,"e":3.72},{"w":"big","s":3.72,"e":4.04},{"w":"one,","s":4.04,"e":4.34},{"w":"what","s":4.68,"e":4.94},{"w":"to","s":4.94,"e":5.24},{"w":"do","s":5.24,"e":5.48},{"w":"with","s":5.48,"e":5.78},{"w":"your","s":5.78,"e":6.08},{"w":"first","s":6.08,"e":6.52},{"w":"ten","s":6.52,"e":6.88},{"w":"thousand","s":6.88,"e":7.34},{"w":"pounds,","s":7.34,"e":7.86},{"w":"or","s":8.32,"e":8.54},{"w":"dollars,","s":8.54,"e":8.86},{"w":"and","s":9.14,"e":9.44},{"w":"how","s":9.44,"e":9.82},{"w":"to","s":9.82,"e":10.04},{"w":"actually","s":10.04,"e":10.66},{"w":"start","s":10.66,"e":11.04},{"w":"investing.","s":11.04,"e":11.62},{"w":"If","s":12.58,"e":12.76},{"w":"you","s":12.76,"e":12.98},{"w":"have","s":12.98,"e":13.32},{"w":"managed","s":13.32,"e":13.62},{"w":"to","s":13.62,"e":14.12},{"w":"save","s":14.12,"e":14.44},{"w":"ten","s":14.44,"e":14.86},{"w":"thousand,","s":14.86,"e":15.38},{"w":"first","s":15.74,"e":16.06},{"w":"of","s":16.06,"e":16.36},{"w":"all,","s":16.36,"e":16.88},{"w":"congratulations.","s":17.08,"e":17.62},{"w":"That","s":18.82,"e":18.92},{"w":"is","s":18.92,"e":19.14},{"w":"a","s":19.14,"e":19.38},{"w":"massive","s":19.38,"e":19.72},{"w":"step.","s":19.72,"e":20.18},{"w":"It","s":20.7,"e":20.9},{"w":"took","s":20.9,"e":21.22},{"w":"me","s":21.22,"e":21.54},{"w":"quite","s":21.54,"e":22.0},{"w":"some","s":22.0,"e":22.34},{"w":"time,","s":22.34,"e":22.84},{"w":"mostly","s":23.22,"e":23.58},{"w":"because","s":23.58,"e":24.08},{"w":"I","s":24.